              }
            ],
            "remarks": "Declare the SBOM's completeness: the 2026 Coverage element expects all components including transitive dependencies, and information gaps must be explicitly stated as unknown or deliberately withheld. This rule verifies the declaration, not actual completeness — the document itself points to external repositories / binary analysis for that. SPDX 2.x has no completeness declaration, so the rule is not evaluated for SPDX 2.x documents. CycloneDX: set compositions\\[\\].aggregate (complete, incomplete, incomplete\\_first\\_party\\_only, …); the first composition is read.",
            "target": {
              "status": {
                "state": "not-satisfied"
              },
              "target-id": "sbom-cisa2026-coverage",
              "type": "objective-id"
            },
            "title": "SBOM-CISA2026-COVERAGE",
            "uuid": "3ee206de-c06a-5bbc-bc57-f0935b9103c4"
          }
        ],
